  "narrative": {
    "intro": "BP Products North America has $413M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The company has 22 awards in the current fiscal year, with an average award size of $18.8M, and obligations are up 566.6% year over year. Historical obligations show a multi-year pattern: FY21 had $510M, FY22 had $1.6B, FY23 had $1.2B, FY24 had $967M, and FY25 had $62M. The FY2026 total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure. The mix of a relatively small award count and a large average award size suggests that BP Products North America is winning fewer but higher-value awards in the current fiscal year. The company’s recent year-over-year swing follows a trough in FY25 and a prior peak in FY22. Contract totals listed in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values rather than current-year obligations. Readers should treat the FY2026 figure as a partial-year snapshot and compare it to full-year values in prior fiscal years when assessing multi-year trends.",
